__pycache__
__clcache__
__cucache__
__hipcache__
__metalcache__
.VSCodeCounter
*.egg-info
.dsh-acl-recovery
.ruff_cache
.pytest_cache
books

# Packaging output. A stray build/ directory is not just clutter: it holds a second
# copy of the package under build/lib/, which ruff then scans, so `python check.py`
# reports hundreds of duplicated findings from the copy until it is removed.
build/
dist/

# Type stubs generated next to handwritten .cl/.cu/.hip kernels on import. The vector-type
# stubs under pygpgpu/vec_types are committed on purpose; these are per-kernel byproducts of
# running examples/ and should not be tracked. The pattern reaches into subdirectories too,
# because a merged kernel_import module writes its stub beside its sources
# (examples/kernel_import/vecops.pyi is such a byproduct).
examples/**/*.pyi
examples/*.pyi

# Editor state. A per-machine .vscode/settings.json records the local interpreter choice,
# which differs between developers and has no bearing on the library.
.vscode/

# The comparison redirects Numba's on-disk cache here through NUMBA_CACHE_DIR, so
# clearing it by name is possible; it is build output, not source.
.numba-cache/
